  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lump sum donation to UN Albania SDG Acceleration Fund &#x2013; Earthquake Recovery Window</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On the 26th of November 2019 Albania was hit by an earthquake (6.3 SvR). The epicenter was 22 km from Durres and 30 km from Tirana. The earthquake caused 51 fatalities and injured at least 913 people. Moreover, up to 17,000 people were displaced due to the loss of their homes.. Experts from the EU, UN and World Bank undertook a Post-Disaster Needs Assessment (PDNA). The total costs of the earthquake are around EUR 1 billion across all sectors, and in 11 affected municipalities. Based on the PDNA, United Nations entities are planning their coordinated contribution to recovery with Government counterparts. UN entities have a wealth of global technical expertise that can be drawn upon for earthquake recovery. UN Albania has opened a dedicated window in the Albania SDG Acceleration Fund to support the UN&#x2019;s system-wide efforts to assist earthquake recovery, as a supplement to the Government&#x2019;s financing mechanism.</narrative>
  </description>
